# Claude Code personal files
CLAUDE.local.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# Conda / virtual envs (in case anyone creates one inside the repo folder)
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Environment / secrets
.env
*.env.local

#folders
notebooks/

# Data
data/raw/
!data/raw/.gitkeep
*.csv
*.parquet

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# Streamlit
.streamlit/

# OS-specific junk (you're on Windows, Eya might not be)
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
A few worth explaining, not just listing:

*.csv broadly, not just data/raw/ — this catches any stray CSV either of you exports anywhere in the repo (a debug output, a quick test file) so it doesn't accidentally get committed. If you ever do need to commit a small CSV on purpose (e.g. your eval test cases), use git add -f path/to/file.csv to force-add past the ignore rule for that one file.
.streamlit/ — Streamlit creates a local config/secrets folder the first time you run it; you don't want that synced between machines.
OS junk for both platforms — you're on Windows (desktop.ini, Thumbs.db), but don't assume Eya is too; .DS_Store covers her if she's on Mac. Costs nothing to include both.
.vscode/ / .idea/ — editor settings are personal, not shared — same logic as CLAUDE.local.md.
Apply it:

bash
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Expand gitignore"
git push origin main
One thing worth checking: if any of these (like a .csv or __pycache__) were already committed before this .gitignore existed, adding the rule now won't remove them retroactively — you'd need git rm --cached <file> for anything already tracked. Worth a quick git status check after this to see if anything unexpected shows as newly-ignored-but-still-tracked.



